    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "$x^2 = 564$. What is the value of $(-x)^2$? Explain how you know.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$564$, because $(-x)^2=x^2$: a number and its opposite have the same square.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(-x)^2&=(-x)(-x)\\\\&=x^2\\\\&=564\\end{align*}$$\nA number and its opposite have the same square.",
